From c6f24e07bbcf0c168dee629bd91ade02d61b0fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Syncony <110027245+Syncony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:14:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(anytls): replay TLS first flight when the session
 dies before answering

Streams whose first bytes are a TLS ClientHello keep up to 64 KiB of
what the app sent until the first response byte arrives. If the session
closes before that, the stream reopens on another session and resends,
at most twice. Plain requests are never replayed, and a stream stops
being replayable as soon as it sends anything but handshake or
change_cipher_spec records, so TLS 1.3 early data never runs twice.
